.TH ATARI-FILE-FORGE 1 "September 2026" "Atari File Forge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
atari-file-forge \- open and maintain Atari media images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atari-file-forge
.RI [ image ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Atari File Forge is a GTK desktop application for browsing, editing,
validating and converting the floppy, hard-disk and ROM images of the Atari
ST, Mega ST, STE, Mega STE, TT030 and Falcon030.
.PP
Files named on the command line are opened through the same private-copy and
format-validation path as the GTK file chooser. Floppies arrive as ST sector
images, MSA or DIM containers, Pasti STX captures, or HFE, SCP and IPF flux.
Hard disks arrive as raw ACSI, SCSI or IDE images carrying an AHDI partition
table, or as a single bare GEMDOS volume.
.PP
HFE floppy images and SCP flux captures are decoded and encoded with the bundled
HxCFloppyEmulator command-line converter, hxcfe. Clean sector-based HFE v1
images are editable and are decoded again for byte-exact verification before
download. Advanced or damaged HFE and SCP images, and every STX image, open
read-only.
.PP
Any open floppy image can be converted to another container with the Export
control in the pane header, or File, Export as. Every such image can be
written back as a plain ST sector image or as MSA; standard 9, 10 and 11
sector geometries can also be wrapped as HFE or SCP. Flux exports are decoded
again and compared byte for byte with the working sectors before the file is
released. The control is disabled for media with no compatible target, such as
a partitioned hard disk.
.PP
With the official Greaseweazle tools installed, the native edition can write an
open floppy image to a connected drive and capture a physical disk back into a
new working image. Captures may be taken as decoded sectors, or as HFE or SCP
flux for disks of unknown condition. A capture is only opened once
Greaseweazle exits cleanly and leaves a usable image, and a failed capture
removes its partial file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ATARI_FILE_FORGE_DISABLE_WEBKIT_SANDBOX
Set to auto, 0 or 1. The default auto mode enables the compatibility fallback
only when Ubuntu reports its restricted unprivileged-user-namespace policy.
.TP
.B ATARI_HATARI_ROOT, ATARI_FILE_FORGE_TOS_DIR, ATARI_FILE_FORGE_CAPSIMAGE
Override the Hatari installation, the directory searched for TOS ROMs you
supply (EmuTOS is bundled and needs no configuration), and the SPS decoder
library used to read IPF captures.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/atari-file-forge/work
Private working images when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I ~/.config/atari-file-forge
Owner identity and atomic client state when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed handbook is under
.IR /usr/share/doc/atari-file-forge/ .
The HFE, SCP and HxCFE guide is
.IR /usr/share/doc/atari-file-forge/handbook/HFE-HXC-GUIDE.md .
